[1.2.6] - 2026-04-29
- Major bot rebalancing across all table formats. Bot vs bot statistics regenerated from millions of simulated hands.
- Fixed two long-standing exploitable leaks: the Loose bot was bleeding chips on Short Handed tables, and the Maniac bot was bleeding on both Full Ring and Short Handed.
- All four gamestyles now play their archetype competitively without a structural exploit on any table format.

[1.2.5] - 2026-04-27
- Smarter bot decisions when stacks get short (going allin if the raise amount would pot-commit the player). 
- Improved defense ranges versus oversized opening raises.

[1.2.4] - 2026-04-25
- added rolling window (25 hands) for replay
- gameplay fixes

[1.2.3] - 2026-04-10
First published Release